      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297559",
      ":question/problem": "The table below shows the distribution of votes for a preferred theme for the school dance in each grade for $80$ students.\n\n| Theme | Freshman | Sophomore | Junior | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Masquerade | $7$ | $8$ | $5$ | $20$ |\n| Galaxy | $6$ | $7$ | $6$ | $19$ |\n| Hollywood | $5$ | $6$ | $5$ | $16$ |\n| Underwater | $9$ | $10$ | $6$ | $25$ |\n| **Total** | **$27$** | **$31$** | **$22$** | **$80$** |\n\nIf one student is selected at random, what is the probability that the student voted for the Galaxy theme?"
